Negative control — the editor's `title` / `description` are re-derived on a
SAVE, not only on a parse (review blocker B1, meta half).

Drops `...deriveMeta(model)` from this module's `setModel`, leaving the model
itself entirely correct. The shared `dataManagerMachine` runs `setMeta` on
`loading.onDone` and on `available.checking.parsing.onDone` — and on NEITHER
`processing.*.onDone`, whose action list is `["setModel", "clearAutoUpdate"]`.
With `allowMultipleEdits` false, `processed` goes straight to `complete`, so
nothing re-enters `parsing` and the meta is never re-derived after a save.
Folding the derivation into `setModel` is what reaches those two limbs without
editing `data-manager.machine.ts`, which is protected core; this mutant undoes
exactly that fold.

The mutant is invisible at every gate that reads the MODEL. The PUT is correct,
the server is correct, the save resolves the saved address, and
`useContext().model` carries the new values. Only the display strings the
manager publishes alongside it are the pre-save ones.

Declared subject — the B1 meta read-back. Open an existing address, change a
field that the meta composes (`name`, or any of address1 / address2 / city /
state / postcode), save, and assert on `useContext()`:
  - `title` reflects the SAVED name/address1
  - `description` reflects the SAVED field order
Under the mutant both still report the form-open address.

What does NOT discriminate:
  - asserting `title` / `description` after `input()` / a plain `SET` — those
    route through `available.checking.parsing`, where the shared machine's own
    `setMeta` still runs. The assertion MUST be taken after a completed save.
  - asserting `useContext().model` — unchanged by the mutant
  - asserting on the create limb only, if the create read-back never inspects
    the meta

Measured blast radius, suite at be4b04cba: ZERO. The whole module suite stays
GREEN under this mutant (115 passed, and the one failure is the standing
